{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And I know</b> נ' (fifty) עקומה (gnomic form): a hint to fifty plagues." "<b>To go</b> — two times in the Masorah in the Torah: here and the other: כי מאן ה' לתתי להלך עמכם. Three were in that counsel: Jethro, Job, and Balaam. The Holy One, blessed be He, said: I know that he will not let you go להלך by Balaam's counsel, and therefore I need to show him My hand to nullify his counsel. And Balaam said: כי מאן ה' לתתי להלך עמכם — to curse the nation."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {1 "The second Masorah citation quotes Numbers 24:11 (בלעם's words to Balak); the third citation in the juxtaposition-reading appears to repeat the same verse, likely as Balaam's own voiced admission."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:50.840525674Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}